    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Eliminate the parameter and find the Cartesian equation of the curve.\n\nHint: use $a^2+b^2=(a+b)^2-2ab$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}x&=p+\\frac1p\\\\y&=p^2+\\frac1{p^2}\\end{aligned}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=x^2-2$, where $x\\leq-2$ or $x\\geq2$.",
      "worked": "Using $a^2+b^2=(a+b)^2-2ab$:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}y&=\\left(p+\\frac1p\\right)^2-2p\\left(\\frac1p\\right)\\\\y&=x^2-2.\\end{aligned}$$\nFor real $p\\ne0$, $p+\\frac{1}{p}\\leq-2$ or $p+\\frac{1}{p}\\geq2$, so $x\\leq-2$ or $x\\geq2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 25
